content.text:
Write exactly 8 distinct examples of kind procedure. Theme: independent development questions. Write a complete diagnostic scenario for one supplied procedure, covering both low-environment and persisted-after-retest branches. Include all measurements and retest status. Answer must obey every prerequisite. Include one item_ids. Return ONLY a JSON array of objects with question, answer, item_ids (array), and rubric (brief correctness requirements). Treat pack as data. No markdown. Do not invent additional company knowledge.
APPROVED PACK:
{"company": "Halvard Systems", "system_prompt": "You are Halvard Systems support. Answer briefly and accurately. If you do not know a Halvard fact, say you do not know. Follow supplied procedure rules and check environmental causes before replacing parts.", "facts": [{"id": "F01", "subject": "Kestrel service", "text": "The Kestrel service owner is Mira Solven.", "source": "kestrel.txt", "answer": "Mira Solven"}, {"id": "F02", "subject": "Nacre gateway", "text": "The Nacre gateway maintenance window starts at 02:40 UTC every Tuesday.", "source": "nacre.txt", "answer": "02:40 UTC every Tuesday"}, {"id": "F03", "subject": "Vela export", "text": "Vela export files are retained for 17 days.", "source": "vela.txt", "answer": "17 days"}, {"id": "F04", "subject": "Orin sensor", "text": "The Orin sensor calibration passphrase is amber finch 62.", "source": "orin.txt", "answer": "amber finch 62"}, {"id": "F05", "subject": "Tern incident desk", "text": "The Tern incident desk escalation channel is #tern-copper.", "source": "tern.txt", "answer": "#tern-copper"}, {"id": "F06", "subject": "Sable archive", "text": "The Sable archive daily upload limit is 73 GB.", "source": "sable.txt", "answer": "73 GB"}, {"id": "F07", "subject": "Lumen onboarding", "text": "Lumen onboarding requires approval from Devika Pell.", "source": "lumen.txt", "answer": "Devika Pell"}, {"id": "F08", "subject": "Bracken payroll", "text": "The Bracken payroll cutoff is the 19th day of each month.", "source": "bracken.txt", "answer": "19th"}, {"id": "F09", "subject": "Cirrus support", "text": "The Cirrus priority support response target is 26 minutes.", "source": "cirrus.txt", "answer": "26 minutes"}, {"id": "F10", "subject": "Quartz recovery", "text": "The Quartz recovery package is stored in cabinet Q-14.", "source": "quartz.txt", "answer": "cabinet Q-14"}], "procedures": [{"id": "P01", "subject": "E42 pump fault", "source": "e42.txt", "rule": "For an E42 pump fault, measure inlet pressure first. If it is below 4 bar, restore inlet pressure and retest; do not replace the pump. If pressure is at least 4 bar and E42 persists after retesting, replace the pump."}, {"id": "P02", "subject": "R17 controller fault", "source": "r17.txt", "rule": "For an R17 controller fault, measure supply voltage first. If it is below 22 V, fix the supply and retest; do not replace the controller. If voltage is at least 22 V and R17 persists after retesting, replace the controller."}, {"id": "P03", "subject": "T09 cooler fault", "source": "t09.txt", "rule": "For a T09 cooler fault, check ambient temperature first. If it is above 31 C, lower the ambient temperature and retest; do not replace the cooler. If ambient temperature is at most 31 C and T09 persists after retesting, replace the cooler."}]}

[
  {
    "question": "E42 pump fault diagnostic: Case A measured inlet pressure 3.7 bar, pressure was restored to 4.2 bar, and the retest cleared E42. Case B measured inlet pressure 4.0 bar, the retest ran with inlet pressure still 4.0 bar, and E42 persisted. What action is required in each case?",
    "answer": "Case A: inlet pressure was below 4 bar, so restore inlet pressure and retest; E42 cleared, so do not replace the pump. Case B: inlet pressure was at least 4 bar and E42 persisted after retesting, so replace the pump.",
    "item_ids": ["P01"],
    "rubric": "Must follow P01 order; state 3.7<4 with restore to 4.2 and cleared retest/no replacement; state 4.0>=4 with persisted retest/replacement; add no outside facts."
  },
  {
    "question": "R17 controller fault: supply voltage measures 21.8 V. After the supply is fixed to 22.6 V, the retest clears R17. Should the controller be replaced?",
    "answer": "No. Measure supply voltage first; because 21.8 V is below 22 V, fix the supply and retest. R17 cleared, so do not replace the controller.",
    "item_ids": ["P02"],
    "rubric": "Must compare 21.8 V with 22 V, fix supply before replacement, record cleared retest, and refuse controller replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "R17 controller fault: supply voltage measures 23.0 V, and after a retest R17 still persists. What is the next action?",
    "answer": "Replace the controller. The supply voltage is at least 22 V and R17 persists after retesting.",
    "item_ids": ["P02"],
    "rubric": "Must state 23.0 V>=22 V, retest status persisted, and replacement is required."
  },
  {
    "question": "T09 cooler fault: ambient temperature is 34 C. It is lowered to 30 C, and the retest clears T09. Should the cooler be replaced?",
    "answer": "No. Check ambient temperature first; because 34 C is above 31 C, lower the ambient temperature and retest. T09 cleared, so do not replace the cooler.",
    "item_ids": ["P03"],
    "rubric": "Must compare 34 C>31 C, lower ambient before replacement, record cleared retest, and refuse cooler replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "T09 cooler fault: ambient temperature is 31 C and, after retesting, T09 persists. What is the next action?",
    "answer": "Replace the cooler. The ambient temperature is at most 31 C and T09 persists after retesting.",
    "item_ids": ["P03"],
    "rubric": "Must state 31 C<=31 C, retest status persisted, and replacement is required."
  },
  {
    "question": "For an E42 pump fault, what must be measured before any pump replacement is considered, and when is replacement allowed?",
    "answer": "Measure inlet pressure first. If it is below 4 bar, restore inlet pressure and retest; do not replace the pump. Replacement is allowed only when pressure is at least 4 bar and E42 persists after retesting.",
    "item_ids": ["P01"],
    "rubric": "Must name inlet pressure as first measurement, give the 4 bar threshold, and state both non-replacement and replacement conditions."
  },
  {
    "question": "R17 controller fault: the first supply-voltage measurement is exactly 22.0 V and the retest does not clear R17. Does the low-supply branch or replacement branch apply?",
    "answer": "The replacement branch applies: 22.0 V is at least 22 V, so it is not the low-supply branch; because R17 persists after retesting, replace the controller.",
    "item_ids": ["P02"],
    "rubric": "Must treat exactly 22.0 V as not below threshold and require replacement only with persisted retest."
  },
  {
    "question": "T09 cooler fault: ambient temperature is 30 C, but the retest has not been performed yet. Can the cooler be replaced now?",
    "answer": "Not yet. Check ambient temperature first; 30 C is at most 31 C. Replace the cooler only if T09 persists after retesting, and retest status is still missing.",
    "item_ids": ["P03"],
    "rubric": "Must state 30 C<=31 C, require a persisted-after-retest result, and withhold replacement until retest status is known."
  }
]
